<h2>What fans see through the ticket partner program</h2>
<p>Your audience will judge the experience, so it is worth knowing what we promise them. Seat Outlet is a resale marketplace, which means prices are set by sellers and may be above or below face value. Our <a href="/ticket-buyer-protection">ticket buyer protection page</a> says orders are covered for valid tickets, delivery before the event, secure payment processing and customer support. If there is a problem with ticket validity, we work to provide replacement tickets of equal or better value, or a full refund. If an event is canceled and not rescheduled, buyers receive a full refund.</p>
<p>For policy wording, see our <a href="/worry-free-guarantee">worry-free guarantee</a> and the <a href="/terms-and-conditions">terms and conditions</a>. Event organizers and venues set their own refund, entry and safety rules, which the terms say usually govern attendance at the event.</p>
<div class="so-callout">
  <p><strong>Honest scope:</strong> This page describes how we talk with partners. It is not an offer, and it does not list guaranteed sales, rates or exclusivity.</p>
</div>

<h2>How to start with the Seat Outlet ticket partner program</h2>
<p>The first step in our ticket partner program is a short conversation. Use the form on our <a href="/ticket-customer-service">ticket customer service page</a> and choose the partnership topic, or email support@seatoutlet.com. A member of our team will follow up to talk through your goals. The form states that we reply within 24 hours.</p>
<p>To make the first call about the ticket partner program useful, prepare a few details:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your event calendar and the venues involved.</li>
  <li>The audience you want to reach.</li>
  <li>Your current ticketing system, if any.</li>
  <li>What a good result would look like for you.</li>
</ul>
<p>While you decide, read our <a href="/blog">blog</a> for industry notes, browse <a href="/buy-tickets-online">the marketplace</a> to see how listings look to fans, and check our <a href="/ticket-faq">ticket FAQ</a> to see what buyers are told.</p>

<h2>Questions about the ticket partner program</h2>
